{"name":"Mutton chops","deep":true,"image":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Mutton_Chops_%282216507576%29.jpg/960px-Mutton_Chops_%282216507576%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","credit":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mutton_Chops_(2216507576).jpg","caption":"Mutton Chops (2216507576)","source":"Wikimedia Commons"},"mentions":0,"casual":{"lead":["Mutton chops are sideburns grown long and wide down the cheeks, usually with the chin shaved. 'Friendly' mutton chops join the sideburns with a moustache. The style is associated with the Victorian era, and with figures such as Civil War general Ambrose Burnside, from whom the word 'sideburns' derives.","For looks, the style frames the face and adds visual width along the jaw and cheeks. Users with a thinner jaw or a patchy chin sometimes choose it because it works with growth on the sides alone."],"sections":[{"h":"How people use it","paras":["People grow side whiskers down the face and keep the chin and neck shaved or trimmed, then maintain the outline with a trimmer or razor. Moustache joining and width are style choices."],"subs":[]},{"h":"Risks & side effects","paras":["Skin irritation or ingrown hairs from shaving around the edges can occur. The style reads as retro, rock or rebellious in some settings, which may or may not be the effect wanted."],"subs":[]}]},"gallery":[{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Mutton_Chops_%282216507576%29.jpg/960px-Mutton_Chops_%282216507576%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","full":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/bb/Mutton_Chops_%282216507576%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","title":"Mutton Chops (2216507576)","license":"CC BY-SA 2.0","creator":"Charles Haynes from Hobart, Australia","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mutton_Chops_(2216507576).jpg","source":"Wikimedia Commons"},{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/07/Mutton_chops_beard_example.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","full":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/07/Mutton_chops_beard_example.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","title":"Mutton chops beard example","license":"CC BY 2.0","creator":"https://www.flickr.com/photos/mariachily/","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mutton_chops_beard_example.jpg","source":"Wikimedia Commons"},{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/69/Mutton_chops_facial_hairstyle_01.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","full":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/69/Mutton_chops_facial_hairstyle_01.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","title":"Mutton chops facial hairstyle 01","license":"CC BY 2.0","creator":"John Markos O'Neill","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mutton_chops_facial_hairstyle_01.jpg","source":"Wikimedia Commons"},{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c1/Old_mutton_chops_-_geograph.org.uk_-_5189978.jpg/960px-Old_mutton_chops_-_geograph.org.uk_-_5189978.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","full":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/c1/Old_mutton_chops_-_geograph.org.uk_-_5189978.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","title":"Old mutton chops - geograph.org.uk - 5189978","license":"CC BY-SA 2.0","creator":"Anthony Vosper","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Old_mutton_chops_-_geograph.org.uk_-_5189978.jpg","source":"Wikimedia Commons"},{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/Mutton_chops.JPG/960px-Mutton_chops.JPG?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_